  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A screen print reproduction of a 1930s travel poster, with two cream aeroplanes over blue waves on a magenta sky and the text City of New York Municipal Airports.",
    "description": "A portrait format screen print in four colours: magenta, cream, blue and dark navy. A cream twin engined aeroplane with pink glowing engine cowls banks across the magenta sky at the top, and a larger cream seaplane with blue underside and a row of portholes sits on stylised blue waves below. The lower third is a blue band with cream art deco lettering reading CITY OF NEW YORK MUNICIPAL AIRPORTS, NO. 1 FLOYD BENNETT FIELD, NO. 2 NORTH BEACH, EAST RIVER SEAPLANE BASES, WALL STREET, 31st STREET, F. H. LaGuardia, John McKenzie. The print shows pinholes and gaps where the stencil did not fully cover.",
    "impression": "A loving copy of a WPA era poster, flaws and all, made to learn how screen printing works. The pink engine glow and the gaps in the ink give it the warmth of a hand pulled print rather than a reproduction. It belongs to the airbrush years' interest in stencils and flat colour.",
